      "text": "Hello, my name is Caleb Levy. I'm a physics PhD student at Harvard, specifically studying astrophysics. So first off, I just wanted to thank the organizers for giving me a chance to share my thoughts today. So my target sidled beyond the buzzword responsibility of platforms in the age of artificial intelligence. So I want to explore our platforms that build and distribute AI systems, especially large-language models, carry not only technical challenges and a driver innovation, but also social responsibilities. And I'll argue that accountability needs to be built into these systems and not bolted on after the fact. I'll also discuss a bit how machine learning and large-language models have impacted some of the research",
