      "text": "towards safer and more useful behavior. There's also this notion of red teaming, which tries to provoke the system to produce dangerous or unhelpful results, so that they can be adjusted before deployment. One example of this is that it would be quite difficult, as I understand it, to convince chat GBT at this point that it's sentient, which I'm personally happy about that one. But the lesson here is important. Is that accountability many times comes only after deployment and public pressure, and after very visible mistakes, and they're not being baked in from the start. And because they're not that predictable, it's difficult to say when you deploy these systems to the world, and more and more users are interacting with it, what kind of behavior is going to emerge.",
