      "text": "to oversight. And when the platforms are the gatekeepers of these models, it really raises the question of the responsibility they have to prevent the harms, given the fact that they're deploying these systems and the accountability of that. So some platforms are taking more steps, transparency reports about training data and its limitations, their accountability frameworks. So who is actually responsible when harm occurs? Different guardrails, like watermarking, generated content, restricting risky API access and integrating fact checking. And perhaps the most important is the partnership with researchers, policymakers, and civil society to monitor risks and prevent harmful actions. So these practices are certainly not perfect, but they're at least showing how platforms can move from being reactive to being more proactive. So where does this leave us?",
