      "fragment_index": 10,
      "start": 484.94,
      "end": 551.24,
      "duration": 66.3,
      "text": "Platforms are not just vendors of tools. They are the gatekeepers of how society interacts with AI. And responsibility means going beyond innovation, just typically profit-driven towards stewardship. And accountability means not only preventing harm before deployment, but also having mechanisms to address harm on when it does happen, and having a clear structure to do so. The truth is that AI is becoming very quickly embedded into the infrastructure of everyday life, and there definitely needs to be creative steps in place to ensure the safety of this infrastructure and to mitigate risks. So I'll just close with this last remark. AI is not just about what these systems can do, and they'll get me wrong. They can do some very incredible things and their behavior, I think, is very fascinating from a research perspective, but it's also about what these platforms allow them to do, and how they've set up frameworks to take responsibility for the consequences.",
